-`end` are midnight UTC and `end` (exclusive) is the start of the day after the last day; the same item cannot be
+Rules: money in integer euro cents; times are ISO-8601 UTC strings; a period of a day or more covers whole days, so `start` and
+`end` are midnight UTC and `end` (exclusive) is the start of the day after the last day; a rental shorter than a day
+starts and ends on the hour and costs `hourlyPrice` for each hour (no discount); an item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour; the same item cannot be
 booked for overlapping periods. Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, …) so behaviour is deterministic.
 A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price (days × `dailyPrice`), rounded to the nearest
 cent with halves rounded up; `quote` and `book` both return the reduced `total`.
